@prefix ds: <https://ds.canonical.com/>.
@prefix anatomy: <https://anatomy.canonical.com/>.
@prefix dt: <https://dt.canonical.com/>.

ds:global.component.chip a ds:Component;
    ds:name "Chip";
    ds:summary "A chip is a compact, interactive component used to represent an attribute, entity, while facilitating secondary actions. Chips elevate specific information in the visual hierarchy, such as categories or selected tags, allowing users to trigger contextual behaviors like filtering, triggering a [Popover](https://docs.superhuman.com/d/_dNyzE_TLZDh#_tugrid-20dWwIHYhx/_rui-i-62pvfoOF), selection, or dismissal. Unlike the [Tag](https://docs.superhuman.com/d/_dNyzE_TLZDh#_tugrid-20dWwIHYhx/_rui-osLY8UcQUp), chips are always actionable. Chips should complement, rather than replace, the primary page actions.\n\n";
    ds:anatomyDsl "";
    ds:anatomyClassic "https://www.figma.com/design/WGHcOmGMEUF9hMAEoRafL8/%F0%9F%93%95-Pragma---documentation-visuals?node-id=2877-8032&t=ch8BFFPUe9gCvMdg-1\n\nStyling\n\nhttps://www.figma.com/design/WGHcOmGMEUF9hMAEoRafL8/%F0%9F%93%95-Pragma---documentation-visuals?node-id=2093-9647&t=ch8BFFPUe9gCvMdg-1\n\n";
    ds:usage "### When to use\n\n- When displaying applied filters in a list, allowing users to see and dismiss active parameters. For example, the [ComboboxField](https://docs.superhuman.com/d/_dNyzE_TLZDh#_tugrid-20dWwIHYhx/_rui-kfEQ25cX4a)  displays selected items inside the input as a dismissible Chip.\n- When displaying a tag, category, or other attributes that a user can interact with. For example, use as a shortcut to filtering. There can be multiple instances of the chip, each representing a different attribute. It is common to find chips located inside of other components such as a table cell, a card, or next to the entity they belong to. \n- When displaying an entity (an object with its own parameters) that needs to trigger a popover for more information. For example, a computer name that would be rendered as a chip and display more details inside a popover when interacted with. \n- When users need to interact with tags, categories, or objects that can be added or removed from a collection.\n\n### When not to use\n\n- If the information is purely read-only (e.g., a \"Status\" indicator), use the [Tag](https://docs.superhuman.com/d/_dNyzE_TLZDh#_tugrid-20dWwIHYhx/_rui-osLY8UcQUp) component instead.\n- Do not use chips for actions on a page, such as \"Submit,\" \"Save,\" or \"Delete All\"; use a [Button](https://docs.superhuman.com/d/_dNyzE_TLZDh#_tugrid-20dWwIHYhx/_rui-8SdtbQUhTr) for these tasks.\n- Chips should not be used as navigation. They should not replace links, the primary navigation menu nor replace [Breadcrumbs](https://docs.superhuman.com/d/_dNyzE_TLZDh#_tugrid-20dWwIHYhx/_rui-BXVe6mKJMd) for structural navigation.\n- If the user needs to input detailed text or data, use a [Field](https://docs.superhuman.com/d/_dNyzE_TLZDh#_tugrid-20dWwIHYhx/_rui-y2LECO9EbF) or [SelectInput](https://docs.superhuman.com/d/_dNyzE_TLZDh#_tugrid-20dWwIHYhx/_rui-xiMRYATXwr) component rather than a series of chips.\n- Avoid using too many chips in a single view if they compete for attention with the primary content of the page.";
    ds:guidelines "Accessibility\n\n## **Color accessibility**\n\n- Chips border colors need to satisfy 3:1 contrast against the lightest/darkest background color state.\n- Use a modifier if it makes sense semantically for your use case.\n- Avoid using semantic color modifiers on top of colored backgrounds.\n- Ensure you don’t use colour as the only visual means of conveying information or an action.\n\n## Alternative text\n\n- There should be an alternative text specified when the value (text) doesn't provide enough contextual information E.g. \"status important\" instead of the default \"important\" as the value of the chip\n\n## Keyboard interactions and focus\n\n- When pressing `Enter` a default chip should perform the filtering action based on its value, the dismissible chip should revert the filtering behavior.\n- When tabulating through chips, the focus area should be the whole chip for the default chip, the dismissible area for the dismissible chip. ";
    ds:tier ds:global;
    ds:documentationStage ds:tag.needsdefinition;
    ds:hasProperty [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "value";
        ds:summary "Controls what the value of the chips is.";
        ds:propertyType "text";
        ds:optional "false"
    ], [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "lead";
        ds:summary "Controls what the lead of the chip is.";
        ds:propertyType "text";
        ds:optional "true"
    ], [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "icon";
        ds:summary "Controls the icon that is shown in the chip.";
        ds:optional "true";
        ds:defaultValue "none"
    ], [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "state";
        ds:summary "The state the button is currently in. ";
        ds:propertyType "choice";
        ds:optional "false";
        ds:defaultValue "default"
    ], [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "color";
        ds:summary "The color the chip should have. Be aware that some of the colors might be interpreted in a semantic way by users. The color token for chips allows input of a hue, and auto generates the correct lightness and chroma. ";
        ds:propertyType "choice";
        ds:optional "false";
        ds:defaultValue "color-foreground-secondary-root"
    ], [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "size";
        ds:summary "Determines the vertical spacing of the chip. Dense can be used in situations where space is limited";
        ds:propertyType "choice";
        ds:optional "false";
        ds:defaultValue "default"
    ], [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "dismissible";
        ds:summary "Determines wether the chip can be dismissed or not. The read-only variant can not be dismissible.";
        ds:propertyType "boolean";
        ds:optional "true";
        ds:defaultValue "false"
    ], [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "badge";
        ds:summary "Can be used to attach a badge to the chip.";
        ds:propertyType "object";
        ds:optional "true";
        ds:defaultValue "none"
    ];
    ds:changeLog [
        a ds:ChangeLogEntry;
        ds:timestamp "2026-02-20T09:00:00.000+01:00";
        ds:change "added initial documentation";
        ds:changeType "change"
    ], [
        a ds:ChangeLogEntry;
        ds:timestamp "2026-05-01T00:00:00.000+02:00";
        ds:change "we decided to not use chips as filters - in the sense as they are the only option to filtering, however, we want the chips to act as a shortcut to a filter: so when clicking on a chip triggers a filter selection ";
        ds:changeType "decision"
    ], [
        a ds:ChangeLogEntry;
        ds:timestamp "2026-05-01T00:00:00.000+02:00"
    ].
